---
title: Buttered stuffing with celery and leeks
servings: 8
tags: [american, vegetarian, thanksgiving, holiday, fall]
cuisine: american
source: Adapted from Buttered Stuffing With Celery and Leeks in tdstein/recipes (MIT), https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tdstein/recipes/main/recipes/Buttered%20Stuffing%20With%20Celery%20and%20Leeks.cook
---

Tear the @sourdough bread{1.25%lb} into 1 1/2- to 2-inch pieces and spread them on a #rimmed baking sheet{}. Leave them uncovered ~{12%hours} to 24 hours to dry.

> No time to dry the bread? Toast the pieces at 300°F until just crisp.

Heat the oven to 375°F.

Warm the @olive oil{1/4%cup} and @unsalted butter{4%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium heat. Add the @garlic{6%cloves}(sliced) and cook until it smells good.

Add the @leeks{2}(chopped) with @salt{} and @black pepper{}. Cook ~{8%minutes} to 10 minutes until soft.

Add the @celery{6%stalks}(sliced) and cook ~{4%minutes} to 6 minutes. Pour in the @dry white wine{1/2%cup} and let it reduce by about three quarters, ~{3%minutes} to 4 minutes. Stir in the @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}.

Whisk the @vegetable stock{2.5%cups} and @eggs{3} in a #medium bowl{}.

In a #large bowl{}, toss the bread with the vegetables, @fresh parsley{1/2%cup}(chopped), @fresh chives{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @fresh thyme{2%tbsp}(chopped). Pour over the egg mixture and toss until it soaks in.

Pile it into a #2 1/2- to 3-quart baking dish{} (a 9-by-13 pan works) and dot with the remaining @unsalted butter{4%tbsp}. Cover with #foil{} and bake ~{25%minutes} to 30 minutes.

Uncover, raise the oven to 425°F and bake ~{20%minutes} to 25 minutes more, until golden and crisp on top.
